.Dd August 5, 2026
.Dt AFPC 1
.Os Netatalk Client
.Sh NAME
.Nm afpc
.Nd control AFP discovery, FUSE mounts, and the stateless controller
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm afpc discover
.Op Fl -verbose | Fl -json
.Op Fl -timeout Ar milliseconds
.Nm afpc sl status | exit
.Nm afpc fs mount
.Op Ar mount-options
.Ar server : volume Ar mountpoint
.Nm afpc fs mount
.Fl -service Ar name
.Op Ar mount-options
.Op Fl -volume Ar volume
.Op Ar mountpoint
.Nm afpc fs unmount | suspend | resume Ar mountpoint
.Nm afpc fs status
.Op Ar mountpoint
.Nm afpc fs exit
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the client-control command. Commands that address a controller always use
an explicit namespace, preventing a command from silently selecting the wrong
controller in installations with both FUSE and stateless AFP operations.
.Pp
.Cm discover
does not contact either controller and is available in every build.
.Pp
.Cm sl
uses the public libafpsl API to communicate with
.Xr afpsld 1 .
It accepts only
.Cm status
and
.Cm exit .
.Pp
.Cm fs
communicates with
.Xr afpfsd 1
and is present only when FUSE support was built. It provides structured
mounting and FUSE mount lifecycle commands. The mount options are the same as
the former AFP client mount command: use
.Fl -service
to resolve an advertised service, and use
.Fl -volume
to select a volume when mounting a service.
.Pp
Unqualified controller commands such as
.Dq afpc status
or
.Dq afpc mount
are invalid. Use the appropriate
.Cm fs
or
.Cm sl
namespace.
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
When FUSE support is built,
.Xr mount_afpfs 1
is installed as a symlink to
.Nm .
Its exact program name selects the AFP-URL mount syntax; it does not accept
.Nm
subcommands.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr afpfsd 1 ,
.Xr afpsld 1 ,
.Xr mount_afpfs 1
